4 CONC n, died at 12:50 p.m. Wednesday (2-28-01) in Countryside Convalescent
Home, East Lackwannock Township, after an extended illness.
She was 96.

Mrs. Spondike was born Sept. 8, 1904, in Wilkes-Barre, Pa
4 CONC ., to Joseph and Helen Hocholak Kenosh. A homemaker, she was a member of St. Michael&#039;s Byzantine Catholic Church, Hermitage. Her husband, Nicholas Spondike Sr., whom she married in June 1926, die
4 CONC d in October 1972.

Surviving are: a son, Nicholas Spondike Jr. and his wife, Alice, West Monroe, La.; a son-in-law, Robert Ross, Hermitage; a brother, Robert Kenosh, Homer City, Pa.; six
grandchildre
4 CONC n, Allyson Spondike, Lone Oak, Texas; Lori Patrick and Jill Porterfield, both Hermitage; Nicholas Spondike III, Spanish Fort, Ala.; Alan and Robert Ross, both Hermitage; and 11 great-grandchildren.

B
4 CONC esides her husband, she was preceded in death by a daughter, Doris M. Spondike Ross, who died in 1999; four brothers, Joe, John, Steve and Andy Kenosh; and three sisters, Ann Brezniak, Sue Sebastian a
4 CONC nd Helen Kenosh.

Memorial contributions may be made to St. Michael Byzantine
Catholic Church, 2230 Highland Road, Hermitage 16148; or United Cerebral Palsy of Middle Tennessee, 209 10th Ave., Suite 1
4 CONC 54, Nashville, Tenn. 37203.

