4 CONC (Kenosh), Veronica Kenosh, Robert Kenosh&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Дополнительная информация: &lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt;LifeSketch: STEVEN E. KENOSH, 58, of 20 Filbert Av
4 CONC e., Homer City, died July 4, 1975 at the Indiana Hospital. A son of Joseph and Helen Hohoyak Kenosh. he was born Nov. 11. 1916 at Ligonier. Mr. Kenosh was a member of the Methodist Church of Homer Cit
4 CONC y. He was well known as an outstanding baseball player, having played professional ball for several years prior to 1941. He had lived almost his entire life in Indiana County. 

Surviving are his wido
4 CONC w, Thelma L. Potts Kenosh; two daughters. Mrs. Richard (Nancy) Tinkey of Murrysville, and Mrs. Edward (Carol) Woehler of Export: four brothers: Joseph of Bedford. Ohio; John, Andrew, and Robert all of
4 CONC  Homer City; three sisters: Mrs. Helen Spondike of Sharon. Ohio; Mrs. John (Ann) Breznick of Farmington, Mich, and Mrs. Steve (Sue) Sebastian of Madison. Ohio. Three grandchildren also survive.
Jul 5,
4 CONC  1975 Indiana Gazette
